# L §5.14.1's table (round 19, writer 10): `bal(x, d start)` "x's balance before day d's movements (d start, §4.6). On
# the decision's day it reads none of that day's movements, its own result included, so it is no cycle; for d after
# that day it is the decision's future, refused as bal(x, d) is" (LOAD-CYCLE where load sees the day, §8.3,
# RUN-FUTURE otherwise). bal(konto, end_of(m) start), the next month's first day, seen at load:
# LOAD-CYCLE (snap14 and this writer's earlier pass: RUN-FUTURE at the read).
=== m.tally
model r
  tally 2
  on 2026-01-01
  start 2026-01-01
  end 2026-12-31

source own "own"
unit PLN: currency minor 0.01
place konto: accounts PLN lives 2020-01-01..
place savings: accounts PLN lives 2020-01-01..
input floor: money PLN
input dom: int

move save[m in months]: transfers
  on start_of(m)
  at start_of(m)
  reads konto
  leg cash from konto to savings amount max(0 PLN, bal(konto, end_of(m) start) - floor)

version v
  cite own
  governs 2026..
  known 2026-01-01
  floor = 100.00 PLN "own"
  dom = 5 "own"
  opening[konto] = 1 000.00 PLN at 2026-01-01 start "statement"

ask s1: bal(savings, 2026-01-31)
=== expect
refused: LOAD-CYCLE save[2026-01] on 2026-01-01 reads bal(konto, end_of(m) start) = 2026-02-01, a later day: its own result or its future (write the projection) (m.tally:14)
